# __STACK__

<One line: what this stack is for.> Builds a `<os>-__STACK__` Tart image; clone
it per-project with `tart-new <name> __STACK__ <os>`.

For host setup, build flow, and daily use, see the [top-level README](../../README.md).
This file documents what's in *this* stack.

## What's in this stack

- **\<runtime\>** — version-managed via mise ([`files/mise.toml`](./files/mise.toml)).

## Customization

- **Tool versions**: [`files/mise.toml`](./files/mise.toml).
- **Stack-specific build deps**: add packages to [`packages.dnf`](./packages.dnf) (Fedora/dnf names), [`packages.apt`](./packages.apt) (Debian/Ubuntu/apt names), and [`packages.brew`](./packages.brew) (Homebrew formula names) — keep all three aligned. [`scripts/00-stack.sh`](./scripts/00-stack.sh) reads the appropriate file for the OS being built.
